    "content": "The directory is empty, so we're starting fresh. Before I build anything, let me get the shape of what you want — a few quick decisions will change the whole architecture:\n\n1. **Platform** — web app, desktop, CLI, or browser extension?\n2. **Scope** — just you (local, single-user) or multiple users with accounts/sync?\n3. **Stack preference** — any language/framework you want (e.g. React, Python/Flask, Go, plain HTML+SQLite)? Or should I pick something sensible?\n4. **Key features beyond basics** — the basics are: add URL, list, delete, edit. Do you also want:\n   - Tags / folders / categories\n   - Full-text search\n   - Auto-fetch page title & favicon\n   - Import/export (e.g. from browser bookmarks)\n\nIf you'd rather not decide all this now, I can just build a **sensible default**: a single-user local web app (Python + FastAPI + SQLite backend, simple HTML/JS frontend) with tags, search, and auto-title-fetch. Fully runnable on your machine, no accounts.\n\nWant me to go with that default, or would you like to adjust any of the above?",
